Templeton Protect — licensing
==============================

The scanning ENGINE and command-line tool are MIT-licensed, under the terms
below. This is everything that finds and explains a finding: mac/Sources/
ProtectCore, mac/Sources/CLI, the exports, and the test suites.

The RESIDENT APPLICATION LAYER — the menu bar presence, scheduled scanning, the
transcript watcher and licence checking — is part of Protect+, a commercial
product. Its source is NOT in this repository; it is kept privately and ships
only inside the signed application. See docs/PRODUCT.md.

It used to be published here. That was honest about what it did and dishonest
about what it cost: anyone could delete the licence check and rebuild, so the
subscription rested on nobody bothering. Removing it is not a claim that the
binary cannot be tampered with — it is the difference between tampering and
recompiling.

Nothing in the MIT engine depends on the resident layer, and the free scanner is
complete on its own. This split is stated here, in the first paragraph, on
purpose — an "open source" badge over a paid core is the misread this project
refuses to earn.

